Route Sheet Activity — Making One Cup of Chai
Available Operations:
Light the stove
Boil water in the pan
Add tea leaves & spices
Simmer till it rises
Strain into the cup
Add milk and sugar
Serve (ship it)
Correct Sequence:
Light the stove → Boil water in the pan → Add tea leaves & spices → Simmer till it rises → Strain into the cup → Add milk and sugar → Serve
Main Concept
This activity teaches the basic idea of programming and algorithms.
A computer follows instructions exactly as written.
The instructions must be given in the correct order.
If the sequence is wrong, the final output will be wrong.
Debugging means finding and correcting mistakes in a program.
Key Point: Writing a sequence of steps for making chai is similar to writing a program—the steps are instructions that must be followed in order.
2. Python Classes
Python classes from Job 07 onward focus on the same idea:
Instructions → Execution → Output → Debugging
The chai activity is like a simple real-life example of how a computer program works.
